## Origin

2026-08-25 - operator hard rule, verbatim:

> Hard Rule: do no use en or em dashes especially in powershell scripts. Create
> a set of rules when building or editing powershell so that they do not always
> fail on first run (look at past errors).

Evidence base, all from this workspace: em dashes making
`Build-PimOfflineServerMsi.ps1` and
`Safe-UpgradeWorkstationAssuranceAgentMsi.ps1` unparseable under Windows
PowerShell 5.1; live mojibake in `Prove-WinrmPrivilegeJob.ps1`; EN DASHes inside
`800-53` and `800-171A` in shipped locale catalogs (about 40 leaves repaired);
`pwsh` resolving to an App Execution Alias stub and raising
`CommandNotFoundException`; bash `for ... do ... done` and `&&` parse failures;
`git show ... >` writing UTF-16LE and producing `UnicodeDecodeError` on byte
`0xff`; inline `python -c` producing `SyntaxError: unterminated string literal`
